\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.  Oh my spirit hark, and rejoice,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 and forget all thy troubles.
\par Hark, thy Master Jesus calls thee,
\par out of the filthness of sin
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Getting out of thy troubles
\par to perpetual good living;
\par what no ear had ever heard of,
\par there thou wilt sojourn forever.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.  Throughout the night, and all day long,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Lord, I did call unto Thee.
\par When my troubles overwhelm me,
\par come and intercede for me.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And just as the traveller
\par expects the end of his trip;
\par so also I look forward that,
\par my troubles and problems shall end.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. As flowers bloom beautifully,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With thorns all over the stem,
\par in the same way that true Christians
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj find themselves amidst problems.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj There is storm, and strong winds blow,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj and rising sea waves that roll;
\par that is how life on earth is like,
\par it's full of troubles and tiresome.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  For this reason, Oh Lord Jesus,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 shine on me, perpetual light.
\par Draw near me and clinch close to me,
\par Let Thy precious blood bathe me.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Out of joy and pleasant life
\par let me depart from this earth.
\par Be my life and light on my path;
\par and kindly be my Good helper.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  I will only expect Thy death,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Through which I shall also die.
\par Owing to the wounds Thou sustained,
\par I shall enter the Kingdom.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj The beautiful Paradise,
\par Thou hast opened all its gates,
\par I shall be ushered in by Thee
\par And I shall stay there forever.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  Hark, Oh my soul and make merry,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 forget about thy troubles;
\par \cf1 for thy Master Jesus calls thee\cf0 
\par to depart from troubled world.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Both glory and joyfulness
\par will ever be thy portion.
\par Thou and the angels will jointly,
\par Sing together songs of praises.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

